plaso.tsv: what plaso (the log2timeline/plaso:20260720 Docker image) reads
from the logs in tests/fixtures/plaso/ with its text/apache_access,
text/confluence_access, text/jira_access and text/bitbucket_access parsers
(psort -o json_line), one line per event: the file, the time (microseconds
since 1970, UTC; Bitbucket's local times as plaso keeps them, as if UTC),
then the values compared, by parser:

- apache_access: address, user, request, status, bytes, referer, user agent,
  virtual host, port;
- confluence and jira: address, user, method, path, protocol, status, bytes,
  referer, user agent, duration (ms), thread, forwarded-for;
- bitbucket: address, user, method, path, protocol, user agent, status,
  bytes read, bytes written, duration (ms), protocol, request id, labels,
  session, SSH repository, mesh execution id.

`-` is written as empty: both read it as no value. Written from plaso's
output, not from this crate.
